From 52b7d58c743dbb4c0ce1e8def39c24299fbb574e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:36:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports: wire MultiTenantRouter + resolver middleware into
 inference path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Activates the per-tenant routing pieces from patches 0011-0016 in the
server boot path, gated by the env var BIFROST_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED
so existing single-tenant deployments observe no behavior change.

Reorganises RegisterInferenceRoutes around a new
buildInferenceRouter(ctx, middlewares) helper:

  off (default):
    returns lib.NewSingleTenantRouter(s.Client) + the unmodified
    middleware chain. No new code path runs for OSS / single-tenant
    deployments.

  on (BIFROST_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED=true|1|yes|on):
    1. builds a TenantLoader closure that queries
       configstore.GetProvidersConfigByTenant (patch 0015) and
       constructs a lib.TenantScopedAccount (patch 0016) per tenant
    2. spawns a multitenant.Manager rooted at s.Ctx so per-tenant
       runtimes drain automatically on shutdown via the Manager's
       built-in ctx-cancel goroutine
    3. wraps the Manager in a lib.MultiTenantRouter with
       FallbackClient=s.Client so requests without a resolved tenant
       id (health probes, /api/platform admin endpoints the resolver
       skips) still serve from the global runtime
    4. prepends handlers.TenantResolverMiddleware (with a 60s
       CachedVKResolver over ConfigStoreVKResolver) so VK→tenant
       lookup happens before every inference middleware downstream

CompletionHandler / AsyncHandler / MCPInferenceHandler are wired
through their *WithRouter constructors added in patch 0014, passing
the resolved router in. The handlers' per-request inference path
still uses h.client directly — the next patch (0018) refactors the
~50 entry-point methods to use h.router.Acquire + defer release so
the Manager's refcount actually pins per-tenant runtimes during
request flight.

Tests:
  4 TestMultiTenantEnabled_* covering the default-off contract,
  truthy variants (1/true/yes/on, case-insensitive), falsy variants
  (0/false/no/off/empty), and surrounding-whitespace tolerance. The
  default-off test is the load-bearing assertion that a future code
  edit can't silently flip the flag on.

Full framework/configstore + plugins/governance + multitenant +
transports/bifrost-http/{handlers,lib,server} test suites pass.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
